/1711269/000171126926000017/evrg-20251231.htm"},"overview":[{"en":"Evergy, Inc., Evergy Kansas Central, Inc. and Evergy Metro, Inc. are separate registrants filing this combined annual report on Form 10-K. The terms \"Evergy,\" \"Evergy Kansas Central,\" \"Evergy Metro\" and \"Evergy Companies\" are used throughout this report. \"Evergy\" refers to Evergy, Inc. and its consolidated subsidiaries, unless otherwise indicated. \"Evergy Kansas Central\" refers to Evergy Kansas Central, Inc. and its consolidated subsidiaries, unless otherwise indicated. \"Evergy Metro\" refers to Evergy Metro, Inc. and its consolidated subsidiaries, unless otherwise indicated. \"Evergy Companies\" refers to Evergy, Evergy Kansas Central, and Evergy Metro, collectively, which are individual registrants within the Evergy consolidated group.","zh":"Evergy, Inc.、Evergy Kansas Central, Inc. 和 Evergy Metro, Inc. 是透過 10-K 表格提交本合併年度報告的獨立註冊人。本報告通篇使用術語「Evergy」、「Evergy Kansas Central」、「Evergy Metro」和「Evergy Companies」。除非另有說明，「Evergy」是指 Evergy, Inc. 及其合併子公司。除非另有說明，「Evergy Kansas Central」是指 Evergy Kansas Central, Inc. 及其合併子公司。除非另有說明，「Evergy Metro」是指 Evergy Metro, Inc. 及其合併子公司。 「Evergy 公司」指 Evergy、Evergy Kansas Central 和 Evergy Metro 的統稱，它們是 Evergy 合併集團內的個人註冊人。"},{"en":"Evergy is a public utility holding company incorporated in 2017 and headquartered in Kansas City, Missouri. Evergy operates primarily through the following wholly-owned direct subsidiaries listed below.","zh":""},{"en":"Evergy Kansas Central, Inc. (Evergy Kansas Central) is an integrated, regulated electric utility that provides electricity to customers in the state of Kansas. Evergy Kansas Central has one active wholly-owned subsidiary with significant operations, Evergy Kansas South, Inc. (Evergy Kansas South).","zh":"Evergy Kansas Central, Inc.（Evergy Kansas Central）是一家受監管的綜合電力公司，為堪薩斯州的客戶提供電力。 Evergy Kansas Central 擁有一家業務活躍的全資子公司 Evergy Kansas South, Inc. (Evergy Kansas South)。"}],"markets":[],"customers":[{"en":"Evergy has approximately 15,800 megawatts (MWs) of owned generating capacity and renewable power purchase agreements. Evergy's owned generation and power purchases from others, as a percentage of total megawatt hours (MWhs) generated and purchased, was approximately 60% and 40%, respectively, over the last three years. About 60% of Evergy's purchased power was purchased under long-term renewable purchased power contracts over the last three years. Evergy purchases power to meet its customers' needs, to satisfy firm power commitments or to meet renewable energy standards. Management believes Evergy will be able to meet its future power purchase needs due to the coordination of planning and operations in the SPP region and existing power purchase agreements; however, price and availability of power purchases may be impacted during periods of high demand or reduced supply.","zh":"Evergy 擁有約 15,800 兆瓦 (MW) 的自有發電能力和再生能源電力購買協議。過去三年，Evergy 自有發電和從其他公司購買的電力佔發電和購買的總兆瓦時 (MWh) 的百分比分別約為 60% 和 40%。 Evergy 約 60% 的外購電力是在過去三年中根據長期再生能源外購電力合約購買的。 Evergy 購買電力是為了滿足客戶的需求、履行堅定的電力承諾或滿足再生能源標準。管理層相信，由於SPP地區規劃和營運的協調以及現有的購電協議，Evergy將能夠滿足其未來的購電需求；然而，在需求高或供應減少期間，購電的價格和可用性可能會受到影響。"}],"competition":[{"en":"Missouri and Kansas continue to operate on the fully integrated and regulated retail utility model. As a result, the Evergy Companies do not compete with others to supply and deliver electricity in their franchised service territories in exchange for agreeing to have their terms of service regulated by state regulatory bodies. If Missouri or Kansas were to pass and implement legislation authorizing or mandating retail choice, Evergy may no longer be able to apply regulated utility accounting principles to deregulated portions of its operations, which may require a surcharge to recover certain costs from legacy customers or could lead to a write-off of certain regulatory assets and liabilities.","zh":"密蘇裡州和堪薩斯州繼續採用完全整合和監管的零售公用事業模式。因此，Evergy 公司不會與其他公司競爭在其特許服務區域供應和輸送電力，以換取同意接受國家監管機構監管其服務條款。如果密蘇裡州或堪薩斯州通過並實施授權或強制零售選擇的立法，Evergy 可能不再能夠將受監管的公用事業會計原則應用於其業務的解除管制部分，這可能需要收取附加費以從傳統客戶收回某些成本，或者可能導致某些監管資產和負債的沖銷。"},{"en":"Evergy competes in the wholesale market to sell power in circumstances when the power it generates is not required for retail customers in its service territory. This competition primarily occurs within the SPP Integrated Marketplace, in which Evergy Kansas Central, Evergy Metro and Evergy Missouri West are participants. This marketplace determines which generating units among market participants should run, within the operating constraints of a unit, at any given time for maximum regional cost-effectiveness.","zh":"當其服務區域內的零售客戶不需要其生產的電力時，Eevery 就會在批發市場上競爭出售電力。這場競賽主要在 SPP 綜合市場內進行，Evergy Kansas Central、Evergy Metro 和 Evergy Missouri West 都是參與者。該市場決定了市場參與者中的哪些發電機組應該在機組的運行限制內運行，在任何給定時間以獲得最大的區域成本效益。"}],"segments":{},"peers":["ES","LNT","PNW","CMS","ATO"]}}